import json,re,sys
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(sys.argv[1]);data={}
CASES={
 'near-far':('A close target and a distant bystander','A Necromancer with Vampire Strike faces a kobold five grids away while a hill giant stands twenty grids away. The closeness scan picks the kobold but leaves its distance variable holding the last entry examined — the giant. The original refuses to cast; the correction judges the chosen kobold and casts.'),
 'near-near':('Control: both monsters close','With a second kobold two grids away both versions cast Vampire Strike. The logs are identical before and after the correction.'),
 'far':('Control: only a distant monster','With only the far hill giant in the list both versions refuse the cast: the chosen distance really is twenty. The logs are identical before and after the correction.')}
for mode,(label,explanation) in CASES.items():
 item={'label':label,'explanation':explanation}
 for phase in ('before','after'):
  raw=(root/f'{phase}-{mode}.log').read_text()
  entry={'raw':raw,'passed':'native-c/vampire-257 finished: 1/1 passed' in raw}
  for tag,key in (('GEOMETRY ','geometry'),('DECISION ','decision'),('OUTCOME ','outcome')):
   match=re.search(re.escape(tag)+r'(.*)',raw)
   entry[key]={k:int(v) for k,v in re.findall(r'(\w+)=(-?\d+)',match[1])} if match else None
  item[phase]=entry
 data[mode]=item
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Vampire Strike judged a bystander's distance</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f4f1ea;color:#253a3c;font:18px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:32px 24px}h1{font-size:40px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:24px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #cbd6d0;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin:18px 0}.cards .card{border-top:6px solid #648e80}.num{font-size:34px;font-weight:750}select,button{font:inherit;max-width:100%;padding:10px;border:1px solid #aabdb5;border-radius:7px;background:white}button{cursor:pointer;margin:14px 8px 0 0}button.active{background:#24685d;color:white}.summary{background:#e6eee6;padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #377367}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:13px/1.5 monospace;max-height:330px;overflow:auto}details{background:white;padding:20px;margin:20px 0}summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:650px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:30px}}</style><main><p>Recorded native Vampire Strike decisions</p><h1>Vampire Strike was judged by a bystander's distance</h1><p>The Borg scans its target list for the closest monster to strike, but the closeness test afterwards reads a variable that the scan left holding the distance of the last entry it examined — including entries it skipped. One distant bystander anywhere in the list kept the spell from ever being cast, even with a perfect target five grids away.</p><section class="card"><label for="scenario">Choose a recorded situation</label><br><select id="scenario"></select><p id="explanation"></p><br><button data-step="0">The target list</button><button data-step="1">The decision</button></section><div class="cards"><section id="original" class="card"><h2>Original</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="action"></p></section><section id="compared" class="card"><h2>Corrected</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="action"></p></section></div><p class="summary" id="outcome"></p><h2>What the controls establish</h2><p>With both monsters close, both versions cast; with only the distant monster, both refuse. Those two complete logs match byte for byte, so the correction changes nothing except the bystander case.</p><details><summary>Experiment conditions and limits</summary><p>Native Human Necromancer level 26, depth 30, seed 1000, lit constructed arena, the Fear and Torment shadow book, Vampire Strike learned as the only spell, full mana, a torch. The production attack chooser acts on its own filled target list; the cast is shown by its queued keys, not executed. This isolates the closeness guard, not full autonomous play; no damage or survival claim.</p></details><details><summary>Recorded native output</summary><h3>Original</h3><pre id="original-log"></pre><h3>Corrected</h3><pre id="compared-log"></pre></details><p>Canonical report: <a href="https://github.com/diegoami/neo-angband-tracker/issues/257">issue257</a>.</p></main><script>
const data=__DATA__;let step=1;const select=document.getElementById('scenario');for(const [key,c] of Object.entries(data)){let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=key;o.textContent=c.label;select.append(o)}function draw(){let c=data[select.value];document.getElementById('explanation').textContent=c.explanation;for(const [panel,phase] of [['original','before'],['compared','after']]){let d=c[phase],p=document.getElementById(panel);p.querySelector('.num').textContent=step===0?`Nearest target ${d.geometry?d.geometry.near:'?'} grids, last listed ${d.geometry?d.geometry.far:'?'} grids.`:`${d.outcome&&d.outcome.cast_spell?'Casts Vampire Strike':'Refuses to cast'} (keys: ${d.outcome?d.outcome.keys:'?'}).`;p.querySelector('.state').textContent=step===0?'The closeness guard should judge the chosen target.':'The chooser fills its own target list.';p.querySelector('.action').textContent=step===1?(d.outcome&&d.outcome.cast_spell?'Spell keys queued.':'No spell cast.'):'';document.getElementById(panel+'-log').textContent=d.raw}document.getElementById('outcome').textContent=select.value==='near-far'?'The original lets the distant bystander veto the strike; the correction judges the chosen target and casts.':'Both versions agree in this control; the logs match byte for byte.';for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.classList.toggle('active',Number(b.dataset.step)===step)}select.addEventListener('change',()=>{step=1;draw()});for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.addEventListener('click',()=>{step=Number(b.dataset.step);draw()});draw();</script></html>'''
(root/'replay.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data).replace('<','\\u003c')))
(root/'replay-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Open in your browser:',root/'replay.html')
